=== SURVEY ===
Date: 2026-04-27T10:27:00-07:00

Backend (internal/api/climate_handler.go):
  - climateMappings had ONLY 4 signals: InsideTemp→inside_temp_c, OutsideTemp→outside_temp_c,
    HvacPower→hvac_state, DefrostMode→defrost_mode
  - Latest endpoint uses SnapshotAt() filtered through climateMappings
  - List endpoint uses SignalTracePivotFlat() with climateMappings, adds created_at + id

Frontend type (web/src/types/vehicle-systems.ts → ClimateState):
  - 35 fields expected: insideTemp, outsideTemp, hvacPower (as number), fanSpeed,
    driverTempSetting, passengerTempSetting, isAcOn, isAutoClimate, climateKeeperMode,
    defrostMode, steeringWheelHeat, seatHeaterLeft/Right/RearLeft/RearCenter/RearRight,
    autoSeatClimateLeft/Right, climateSeatCoolingFrontLeft/Right, seatVentEnabled,
    overheatProtection, batteryHeater, etc.
  - Types used camelCase (works via camelCaseKeys transform in resilience.ts)

Frontend page (ClimateControlPage.tsx, 1269 lines):
  - Uses ALL ClimateState fields across gauges, cards, charts, data table
  - Efficiency stats computed hvacPower as numeric kW — wrong (HvacPower is TypeEnum string)
  - steeringWheelHeat used as boolean — no direct signal exists

signal_types.go — Available climate signals (31 total):
  InsideTemp(float), OutsideTemp(float), HvacLeftTemperatureRequest(float),
  HvacRightTemperatureRequest(float), HvacPower(enum), HvacACEnabled(bool),
  HvacAutoMode(enum), HvacFanSpeed(float), HvacFanStatus(float),
  ClimateKeeperMode(enum), DefrostMode(enum), DefrostForPreconditioning(bool),
  RearDefrostEnabled(bool), WiperHeatEnabled(bool), RearDisplayHvacEnabled(bool),
  BatteryHeaterOn(bool), CabinOverheatProtectionMode(enum),
  CabinOverheatProtectionTemperatureLimit(enum), HvacSteeringWheelHeatAuto(bool),
  HvacSteeringWheelHeatLevel(float), SeatHeaterLeft(float), SeatHeaterRight(float),
  SeatHeaterRearLeft(float), SeatHeaterRearCenter(float), SeatHeaterRearRight(float),
  AutoSeatClimateLeft(bool), AutoSeatClimateRight(bool),
  ClimateSeatCoolingFrontLeft(float), ClimateSeatCoolingFrontRight(float),
  SeatVentEnabled(bool)

camelCaseKeys (web/src/lib/resilience.ts):
  - Keeps original snake_case key AND adds camelCase key
  - e.g. inside_temp → both inside_temp and insideTemp available
  - Field names must be chosen so snake_case → camelCase matches frontend type

=== REASONING ===

Root causes:
1. Backend only mapped 4 of 31 available climate signals
2. Backend field names (inside_temp_c, hvac_state) didn't match frontend expectations
   after camelCaseKeys (insideTempC ≠ insideTemp, hvacState ≠ hvacPower)
3. Frontend type had hvacPower as number, but HvacPower is TypeEnum (string)
4. Frontend type had steeringWheelHeat boolean with no backing signal
5. Frontend type had isAutoClimate boolean, but HvacAutoMode is TypeEnum (string)
6. Efficiency stats treated hvacPower as kW — fabricated metric (ADR-002 violation)

Fix approach:
- Backend: expand climateMappings to 31 signals with field names that produce correct
  camelCase after transform (inside_temp→insideTemp, driver_temp_setting→driverTempSetting)
- Backend: add timestamp alias in List handler for frontend chart/table compat
- Frontend type: update ClimateState to match actual signal types (hvacPower→string,
  all fields optional since signals may not be present)
- Frontend type: remove steeringWheelHeat (derive from level), isAutoClimate→hvacAutoMode
- Frontend page: null-safe all field accesses, replace fabricated kW stats with
  fan speed stats + AC on-time %, replace hvacPower chart area with AC state binary

